WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.971
Resignation Conversation.

2
00:00:02.251 --> 00:00:05.835
Day 90 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:08.609
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.889 --> 00:00:11.791
People remember how you left more than how you joined.

5
00:00:12.071 --> 00:00:20.711
Make the decision first, tell your manager before anyone else, be grateful and brief, hand over properly, and leave everyone glad they worked with you.

6
00:00:22.061 --> 00:00:22.914
Part 1.

7
00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:24.559
The resignation path.

8
00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:26.727
Step 1:

9
00:00:27.007 --> 00:00:30.868
Decide: offer letter signed; you're sure; you know your notice period.

10
00:00:31.148 --> 00:00:32.065
Step 2:

11
00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:36.356
Tell your manager: in person or on video, never first by email.

12
00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.553
Step 3:

13
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:41.161
Put it in writing: short, polite resignation email.

14
00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.401
Step 4:

15
00:00:42.681 --> 00:00:45.839
Handle the counter-offer: decide beforehand what you'll do.

16
00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:47.079
Step 5:

17
00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:50.793
Serve the notice: hand over, document, stay professional.

18
00:00:51.073 --> 00:00:52.012
Step 6:

19
00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:55.385
Exit well: exit interview, farewell, stay connected.

20
00:00:56.735 --> 00:00:57.610
Part 2.

21
00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.682
Before you resign: checklist.

22
00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:04.729
Signed offer letter from the new company (not just a verbal offer).

23
00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:08.252
Notice period and buyout rules checked in your contract.

24
00:01:08.532 --> 00:01:14.121
Unused leave, pending bonus or ESOP vesting dates checked; is it worth waiting a few weeks?

25
00:01:14.401 --> 00:01:20.119
Personal files removed from company devices (only personal files, never company data).

26
00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:22.703
Your reason in one positive sentence.

27
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:25.116
Your answer to a counter-offer decided.

28
00:01:26.466 --> 00:01:27.362
Part 3.

29
00:01:27.642 --> 00:01:28.858
Telling your manager.

30
00:01:30.108 --> 00:01:31.367
Asking for the meeting.

31
00:01:31.647 --> 00:01:32.585
You could say:

32
00:01:32.865 --> 00:01:36.535
Hi Priya, do you have 15 minutes today for a private conversation?

33
00:01:36.815 --> 00:01:38.948
Something I'd like to discuss in person.

34
00:01:40.298 --> 00:01:41.365
The conversation.

35
00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:42.583
You could say:

36
00:01:42.863 --> 00:01:44.335
Thank you for making time.

37
00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:46.109
I've decided to resign.

38
00:01:46.389 --> 00:01:52.895
I've accepted an offer from another company, and my last working day would be 3rd February, per my notice period.

39
00:01:53.175 --> 00:01:54.797
This wasn't an easy decision.

40
00:01:55.077 --> 00:02:01.562
I've learned a lot here, especially from you: the checkout migration and leading the team were big growth steps for me.

41
00:02:01.842 --> 00:02:04.743
I want to make the transition as smooth as possible.

42
00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:07.242
I'll prepare a handover plan by Friday.

43
00:02:08.592 --> 00:02:10.661
Keep it short, positive and final.

44
00:02:10.941 --> 00:02:13.373
You're informing them, not asking permission.

45
00:02:14.723 --> 00:02:16.814
\Why are you leaving?\.

46
00:02:17.094 --> 00:02:18.033
You could say:

47
00:02:18.313 --> 00:02:25.587
It's an opportunity to work on larger-scale systems and move into an architect role, which is the direction I want to grow in.

48
00:02:26.937 --> 00:02:29.177
One positive, forward-looking reason.

49
00:02:29.457 --> 00:02:32.508
Don't list complaints in this meeting, even if you have them.

50
00:02:32.788 --> 00:02:36.649
Save constructive feedback for the exit interview, and keep it gentle.

51
00:02:37.999 --> 00:02:40.005
\Where are you going?\.

52
00:02:40.285 --> 00:02:41.223
You could say:

53
00:02:41.503 --> 00:02:45.770
I'd prefer to share that closer to my last day, once everything is finalised.

54
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.373
I hope you understand.

55
00:02:48.723 --> 00:02:50.771
or simply tell them if you're comfortable.

56
00:02:51.051 --> 00:02:52.096
Both are fine.

57
00:02:53.446 --> 00:02:55.003
Manager reacts badly.

58
00:02:55.283 --> 00:02:56.222
You could say:

59
00:02:56.502 --> 00:03:00.406
I understand this comes at a hard time, and I'm sorry about the timing.

60
00:03:00.686 --> 00:03:06.169
I'm committed to a proper handover and will do everything I can to reduce the impact on the team.

61
00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:08.479
Stay calm.

62
00:03:08.759 --> 00:03:11.276
Don't argue or justify yourself at length.

63
00:03:12.626 --> 00:03:13.543
Part 4.

64
00:03:13.823 --> 00:03:15.317
The resignation email.

65
00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.444
Here is a template you can copy.

66
00:03:18.724 --> 00:03:19.599
Subject:

67
00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:21.820
Resignation, Ashish Gupta.

68
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.017
Dear Priya.

69
00:03:23.297 --> 00:03:28.972
Please accept this email as formal notice of my resignation from my position as Senior.

70
00:03:29.252 --> 00:03:32.089
Software Engineer at XYZ Technologies.

71
00:03:32.369 --> 00:03:35.783
As per my notice period, my last working day. will be.

72
00:03:36.063 --> 00:03:38.516
3 February 2027.

73
00:03:38.796 --> 00:03:42.359
Thank you for the opportunities and support over the past four years.

74
00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:48.057
I'm grateful for. everything I've learned here, and I'll do my best to ensure a smooth handover.

75
00:03:48.337 --> 00:03:49.404
Best regards.

76
00:03:49.684 --> 00:03:51.753
The rest of the template is on the page.

77
00:03:54.603 --> 00:03:56.737
Keep it short, factual, and grateful.

78
00:03:57.017 --> 00:03:58.745
No reasons, no complaints.

79
00:03:59.025 --> 00:04:01.883
This email goes into your permanent HR record.

80
00:04:03.233 --> 00:04:04.193
Part 5.

81
00:04:04.473 --> 00:04:05.924
Handling the counter-offer.

82
00:04:07.174 --> 00:04:08.518
Here is a quick table:

83
00:04:08.798 --> 00:04:10.313
Question, and Think about.

84
00:04:10.593 --> 00:04:12.022
Why did I start looking?:

85
00:04:12.302 --> 00:04:15.267
Will more money fix that (manager, growth, tech, culture)?

86
00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:17.190
Why is the offer coming now?:

87
00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.966
Why wasn't I valued this way before I resigned?

88
00:04:20.246 --> 00:04:21.462
How will I be seen?:

89
00:04:21.742 --> 00:04:24.281
Some leaders will now see you as a flight risk.

90
00:04:24.561 --> 00:04:25.905
What about the new company?:

91
00:04:26.185 --> 00:04:29.641
Backing out after accepting damages your reputation there.

92
00:04:30.991 --> 00:04:32.548
Declining the counter-offer.

93
00:04:32.828 --> 00:04:33.767
You could say:

94
00:04:34.047 --> 00:04:38.633
Thank you, I really appreciate the offer, and it means a lot that you want me to stay.

95
00:04:38.913 --> 00:04:41.409
I've thought carefully, and I've made my decision.

96
00:04:41.689 --> 00:04:45.295
My reasons are about the role and growth, not just compensation.

97
00:04:46.645 --> 00:04:48.522
If you genuinely want to consider it.

98
00:04:48.802 --> 00:04:49.741
You could say:

99
00:04:50.021 --> 00:04:50.853
Thank you.

100
00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.714
Can I have until tomorrow to think it over?

101
00:04:53.994 --> 00:04:56.362
I want to make the right decision for everyone.

102
00:04:57.712 --> 00:05:00.592
Be honest with both companies and decide quickly.

103
00:05:01.942 --> 00:05:02.881
Part 6.

104
00:05:03.161 --> 00:05:05.038
Notice period: leaving well.

105
00:05:06.288 --> 00:05:12.581
Handover document: systems you own, credentials process, ongoing work, known issues, contacts.

106
00:05:12.861 --> 00:05:15.613
Knowledge-transfer sessions recorded for the team.

107
00:05:15.893 --> 00:05:20.139
Finish or cleanly hand over in-progress tickets; don't start big new work.

108
00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:23.469
Update runbooks or READMEs for anything only you know.

109
00:05:23.749 --> 00:05:26.011
Stay fully engaged until your last day.

110
00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:27.400
People notice.

111
00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.821
Ask about a notice buyout or early release politely if the new company needs you sooner.

112
00:05:34.171 --> 00:05:35.110
You could say:

113
00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.849
Would it be possible to be released on 20th January instead of 3rd February?

114
00:05:40.129 --> 00:05:46.038
I've planned the handover so it would be complete by then, and I'm happy to be available for questions afterwards.

115
00:05:47.388 --> 00:05:48.327
Part 7.

116
00:05:48.607 --> 00:05:49.737
Exit interview.

117
00:05:50.987 --> 00:05:52.651
Be honest but constructive.

118
00:05:52.931 --> 00:05:55.043
Focus on systems, not people:

119
00:05:56.393 --> 00:05:57.737
Here is a quick table:

120
00:05:58.017 --> 00:05:59.511
Avoid, and Say instead.

121
00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:01.391
My manager is terrible.:

122
00:06:01.671 --> 00:06:05.447
More regular feedback and clearer growth paths would help people stay.

123
00:06:05.727 --> 00:06:07.284
Everything here is broken.:

124
00:06:07.564 --> 00:06:10.508
Investing in on-call tooling would reduce burnout.

125
00:06:10.788 --> 00:06:12.111
The pay is a joke.:

126
00:06:12.391 --> 00:06:16.103
Compensation was below market for my role, which was a factor.

127
00:06:17.453 --> 00:06:18.327
Part 8.

128
00:06:18.607 --> 00:06:19.823
Farewell message.

129
00:06:21.073 --> 00:06:22.951
Here is a template you can copy.

130
00:06:23.231 --> 00:06:24.276
Hi everyone.

131
00:06:24.556 --> 00:06:26.689
Today is my last day at XYZ.

132
00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:28.655
It's been an amazing four years.

133
00:06:28.935 --> 00:06:35.740
I've learned so much. from this. team, from late-night sale days to the checkout migration we pulled off together.

134
00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:39.348
Thank you for the support, the code reviews, and the chai breaks.

135
00:06:39.628 --> 00:06:40.695
I'll miss you all!

136
00:06:40.975 --> 00:06:47.247
Let's stay in touch: linkedin.com or in or ashish-example, ashish.personal@example.com.

137
00:06:47.527 --> 00:06:48.487
All the best.

138
00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:49.599
Ashish.

139
00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:53.345
Part 9.

140
00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:54.414
Don'ts.

141
00:06:55.664 --> 00:06:56.581
Watch out:

142
00:06:56.861 --> 00:06:57.565
Never.

143
00:06:57.845 --> 00:07:01.429
Announce your resignation to the team before your manager knows.

144
00:07:01.709 --> 00:07:06.659
Post about it on LinkedIn before your last day (or before your manager agrees on timing).

145
00:07:06.939 --> 00:07:11.163
Take company code, documents or customer data, even for reference.

146
00:07:11.443 --> 00:07:14.941
Badmouth the company or colleagues, in the office or online.

147
00:07:15.221 --> 00:07:19.019
Mentally check out during notice; it's the last thing people remember.

148
00:07:19.299 --> 00:07:22.243
Try to recruit teammates to your new company during notice.

149
00:07:23.593 --> 00:07:24.446
Part 10.

150
00:07:24.726 --> 00:07:26.987
For team leads: when someone resigns.

151
00:07:28.237 --> 00:07:31.309
Thank them and congratulate them, even if it hurts:

152
00:07:31.589 --> 00:07:34.128
I'm sad to lose you, but this is a great step.

153
00:07:34.408 --> 00:07:38.909
Ask once if there's anything that would change their mind, then respect the answer.

154
00:07:39.189 --> 00:07:39.851
Ask:

155
00:07:40.131 --> 00:07:41.517
What could we have done better?

156
00:07:41.797 --> 00:07:43.227
Listen; don't defend.

157
00:07:43.507 --> 00:07:47.517
Plan the handover together and tell the team with them, in a positive way.

158
00:07:47.797 --> 00:07:49.120
Celebrate their exit.

159
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.112
Alumni can become referrals, clients, or future re-hires.

160
00:07:54.462 --> 00:07:55.465
Part 11.

161
00:07:55.745 --> 00:07:57.131
Practice conversation:

162
00:07:57.411 --> 00:07:58.627
Telling your manager.

163
00:07:59.877 --> 00:08:01.904
Here is how the conversation goes.

164
00:08:02.184 --> 00:08:03.848
Thanks for making time.

165
00:08:04.128 --> 00:08:07.840
I wanted to tell you in person that I've decided to resign.

166
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:08.803
Oh.

167
00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:10.341
That's a surprise.

168
00:08:10.621 --> 00:08:11.901
Can I ask why?

169
00:08:12.181 --> 00:08:16.619
I've accepted an offer to work on larger systems in an architect role.

170
00:08:16.899 --> 00:08:19.288
It's the direction I want to grow in.

171
00:08:19.568 --> 00:08:20.933
I'm sad to lose you.

172
00:08:21.213 --> 00:08:23.325
Is there anything that would change your mind?

173
00:08:24.675 --> 00:08:26.275
The conversation continues.

174
00:08:26.555 --> 00:08:29.926
I really appreciate that, but I've made my decision.

175
00:08:30.206 --> 00:08:33.193
I've learned so much here, especially from you.

176
00:08:33.473 --> 00:08:35.009
When would your last day be?

177
00:08:35.289 --> 00:08:38.041
The 3rd of February, as per my notice.

178
00:08:38.321 --> 00:08:40.945
I'll prepare a handover plan by Friday.

179
00:08:41.225 --> 00:08:42.334
Thank you.

180
00:08:42.614 --> 00:08:44.513
Let's plan the transition together.

181
00:08:45.863 --> 00:08:47.399
That's the end of this lesson.

182
00:08:47.679 --> 00:08:52.329
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

183
00:08:52.609 --> 00:08:58.732
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

